00:06:14,265 --> 00:06:19,670
and it's still code that is then handed off to uh a player like Broadcom.

77
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:26,883
Um and so, you know, that kind of front-end design that describes the kind of underlying intent of the chip, the underlying logic of the chip,

78
00:06:26,933 --> 00:06:32,494
is then transformed ultimately into something that, you know, what gets shipped to TSMC in the end is literally a kind of bitmap.

79
00:06:32,544 --> 00:06:36,950
Uh you know, we would have this file type you call GDS2, and it's literally,

