00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,985
you know, where do I put the metal layers, where do I put each individual transistor.

81
00:06:41,035 --> 00:06:42,819
And so, it's a it's a full layout.

82
00:06:42,869 --> 00:06:50,691
And so, you go through this process of synthesis of that RTL into a kind of set of circuits that then ultimately get laid out.

83
00:06:50,741 --> 00:06:56,406
And a lot of the complexity there is around um you know, in Broadcom's case, you know,

84
00:06:56,456 --> 00:07:01,392
it would be ownership of analog IP that is used for chip-to-chip connectivity.

85
00:07:01,442 --> 00:07:07,252
And it is this kind of physical placement that is specific to a given process node at TSMC.

86
00:07:07,302 --> 00:07:11,947
So, you know, we talk about like 3 nanometers, 5 nanometers, et cetera.

87
00:07:11,997 --> 00:07:18,070
